A||N||11||Seanh||T-6 Turbo :)||||7||
Z||000000||Seanh||08-31-2001||07:52 PM||||Today I was commin' back from school and some dude and his riced honda pulled up and said he'd heard my Fiero was a pretty fast car around town, so he wanted to race. Me being one to never turn down a race even if I know I'm gonna get stomped, said lets go. I'd seen this car flying around town before, and never saw anything beat it. Its a 1.6L 4 banger that will smoke 1st, 2nd, and 3rd, and bark into 4th and 5th, highly modified I assume. It was pretty damn fast, but I still smoked him. Then we get to talkin' afterwards and he mentions he has a T-6 turbo setup for a 3.8L Grand National engine, manifold and all, that he needs to get rid of. I am pretty sure that its a 90 degree engine, right? He said the top (plenum) looks the same and he thinks it will bolt up perfectly. So do you think it would work on my engine? Maybe the manifold would have to be changed out, but the actual turbo and most of the components would work right? I really would love to have this bad boy, and will probally talk to him in the next week about buying it, so I need to know. Also how much would a manifold and whatever else I need to do this cost me? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto (Currently in repair, wrecked by "Red-Headed Step Child")<BR><I>I live my life a 1/4 mile at a time. Nothing else matters</I>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Shaun41178||08-31-2001||08:13 PM||||The intake will not bolt up.<P>But the turbo could be used.  That would be a nice turbo too to have.  Yea some people will say it is too big but you have a 3.4 right?  Put it on a 3.4  Heck even if you have a 2.8 put it on that.  You will have some lag.  I will say full boost won't hit till about 4k rpm with the 2.8.  You will have boost from like 2500 rpm though 7k easy with that turbo but full boost probably not till around 4k.  That size turbo will flow a ton of air for your engine and hardly be working meaning it will keep the intake temps down allowing you to run more boost without needing an intercooler.   It will allow you to flow more air then a T-3 that everyone and their mother uses on this board, which IMO is too small, so you could make the same amount of power with that turbo at less boost keeping the engine in so called "safe zone".  Use a nice 2.5 inch downpipe to a 2.5-3 inch exhaust on that bad boy and hold on tight.  Get some nice electronics like wastegate controllers to adjust boost.  Aftermarket ignition to adjust timing and a rising rate FPR to add more fuel.<P>Want the turbo to spool up faster then put a 40 shot of nitrous on it from 2k rpm to 3500 rpm.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||09-01-2001||01:16 AM||||T-6 DO NOT EXIST!!!!!  The GN rngine use a T60, is a v6 90* engine. To use it you will need a kit like the one archie sales.  Also the parts from both egines CANT be interchangeable. You can use the turbo and some parts. Your best bet is get a kit from archie and use it all. Do a search in the tach forum for Grand National or GN.<P>Hope helps<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||09-01-2001||01:48 AM||||DreXter, I don't think he meant that it was a complete GN engine. It's just the turbo parts. <P>I don't know how the guy could mistake a Turbo Buick plenum for a Fiero one either.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||09-01-2001||11:49 AM||||I need to talk to him more, but I am now thinking he meant the entire manifold, like all 3 planes on the Fiero setup, was what he had and thought would work on this engine, but it won't since I'm pretty sure its a 90* engine, not 60* like mine. About the comment on the T-6 and T-60, the guy who was with me seems to think he said it was a T-60 turbo, I however thought he said T-6, so I'll have to find out for sure what he really has. What else would have to be done to the Fiero intake to use the turbo. What manifold should I use and where to get it cheapest? I think I'm gonna buy, so this will be a real interesting project, until I blow my engine again that is....<P>Yeah, this will be going on the 3.4.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||09-01-2001||09:53 PM||||You could use the stock Fiero intake, the turbo and a few other parts. But you can't use the manifolds (intake or exhaust) and probably won't be able to use the pipes leading from the turbo to the intake.<BR>Basically you would have to do a custom setup similar to the other turbo installs for Fieros (Dennis LaGrua for examlpe) but using all of the buick parts you can. If you are going to get it. Get everything so you have all of it to work with. Then sell what you don't use.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||09-02-2001||12:35 AM||||I did talk to a friend of his tonight, and he said he's sure it came off a Grand National, but unsure what engine was in it, so if anyone knows what they have...<P>He'll sell the whole setup for like $600, so I said yes, and I'll have it pretty soon. Can't wait now!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Leper||09-02-2001||01:12 AM||||All Grand Nationals are turbo 3.8's and I'm 99% sure that they were all fuel injected. (Buick made some carbed turbo 3.8's too, but I think the GN came out after they swithched to EFI)||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||09-02-2001||02:25 AM||||PERFECT turbo (well, for ultimate performance at least, you will have lag, but that's what makes turbo cars FUN and intresting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> for the 3.4!!<P>You will likely end up pretty much building a custom setup around the two turbines, but boy is it going to be fast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (If you don't know the difference between a blowoff valve and a wastegate, or between a boost-timing unit, and ajustable boost controler, have a pro build it, or spend a few months learning  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> I'd go the full electronics route, and make it an ultimate balls-out manifold glowing turbo pavement eating machine, you have the right turbine for it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>I did talk to a friend of his tonight, and he said he's sure it came off a Grand National, but unsure what engine was in it, so if anyone knows what they have...<P>He'll sell the whole setup for like $600, so I said yes, and I'll have it pretty soon. Can't wait now!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||hugh||09-02-2001||08:22 AM||||The 82 GN was not turbocharged.The 84/85 were not intercooled.The 86/87 were intercooled.I don't know for sure about the 82(4.1L),but 84 through 87(3.8L) were SFI.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||09-02-2001||01:50 PM||||I only know pretty basic stuff about turbos and seting them up. I'v only messed with ones already installed, never installed one of my own. Anyone know of some websites that might be helpful on either turbo's in general, or installing them on a Fiero please post them. I am going to check into how much someone would charge to install it, but if its much I will give it a try myself, it can't be THAT difficult, right?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||RedOktober||09-03-2001||06:04 AM||||I wpuld recommend for everyone to go and get the latest issue of Sports Compact. They have a great article in there about how to properly size ur turbo to the engine. It is too lonk for me to repoast it here, but I feel it is worth the time to read. <P>From My friend's 87 GNX, I feel this turbo is a bit large for the 2.8.  But if you have a 3.4, Go for It...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-004S_1.JPG"> <BR>You will have a bit of lag, But an adjustment to the wastegate by a pepcock valve can help that. I would suggest trying to find a MR2 Intercooler from a Supercharged car (88ish) or one from a turbo 323(86-88) or MR2 to help cool your charged air.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-005S_1.JPG"> <BR>That big black cast iron thing down there is an upgraded IC.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-011S_1.JPG"> <BR>This is a MR2 IC with a Motorcycle fan on it .. Good for 15 PSI on pump gas. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red6[1]a.jpg"> <BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
